Title: Apache Traffic Server

# Welcome to Apache Traffic Server!

Apache Traffic Server™ is a powerful, versatile HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 compliant caching proxy server. Originally a commercial product, it was generously donated to the Apache Foundation by Yahoo! and is now utilized by numerous major CDNs and content owners.

Explore our features, get support, and join the community to leverage the full potential of Apache Traffic Server.

---

## Get Started

### [Downloads](/downloads)

Get the latest version of Apache Traffic Server.

### [Follow @trafficserver](https://twitter.com/trafficserver)

Stay updated with the latest news and announcements.

---

## Key Features

### Caching

Enhance response time, reduce server load, and minimize bandwidth consumption by caching frequently-requested web pages, images, and web service calls.

### Proxying

Effortlessly implement keep-alive, content filtering, anonymization, or load balancing through a flexible proxy layer.

### Fast

Designed to scale efficiently on modern SMP hardware, capable of handling tens of thousands of requests per second.

### Extensible

Utilize APIs to develop custom plugins for tasks ranging from HTTP header modification to implementing bespoke cache algorithms.

### Proven

Battle-tested at Yahoo!, processing over 400TB of data daily as both forward and reverse proxies. Explore our [Customers page](users.html) for insights into our corporate users and supporters.

---

## Learn More

### Get Support

#### Users Mailing List & Slack Channel

Subscribe to our Users Mailing List or join our **#traffic-server** channel on [The ASF Slack](https://the-asf.slack.com/). Reach out for assistance with builds, configurations, or any questions.

#### Developers & Bug Tracking

Join our dev discussion list for help with plugin development or code-related inquiries. Report or confirm bugs through our [Bug Tracker](https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/).

#### Useful Resources

Learn how to ask effective questions, create informative bug reports, and apply patches efficiently.

### Get Involved

#### Community Engagement

Participate in our users and developers mailing lists. Share your experiences or seek assistance on our Slack channel.

#### Contribution & Development

Contribute to ongoing projects, create patches, or debug Apache Traffic Server. Explore beginner-friendly tasks tagged in our GitHub issues.

### Web Resources

- **[Administrator's Guide](https://docs.trafficserver.apache.org/en/latest/admin-guide/index.en.html):** Installation, configuration, and administration guidelines.
- **[Developer's Guide](https://docs.trafficserver.apache.org/en/latest/developer-guide/index.en.html):** Insights into plugin development and underlying code mechanisms.
- **[Frequently Asked Questions](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/TS/FAQ):** Answers to common queries and troubleshooting tips.
- **[Wiki](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/TS/Apache+Traffic+Server) and [Blog](https://blogs.apache.org/trafficserver/):** Collaboration platforms and project insights.

